🧠 Sentiment Analysis Using NLP

Welcome to my Sentiment Analysis project! This repository showcases how machine learning and NLP can be used to analyze textual data and classify sentiments (Positive, Negative, Neutral) — ideal for customer reviews, social media analysis, and more.


🚀 Features

✅ Preprocessing pipeline (stopwords removal, lemmatization, tokenization)

🔍 Sentiment classification using models like Logistic Regression, SVM, and BERT

📊 Visualizations (word clouds, polarity distributions, confusion matrix)

🗣️ Real-time text input with web UI via Gradio

🌐 Support for multiple languages (optional with pre-trained multilingual models)


🛠️ Tech Stack

Language: Python 🐍

Libraries: NLTK, spaCy, Scikit-learn, Matplotlib, Seaborn, Transformers (HuggingFace)

Model: Logistic Regression | BERT | DistilBERT

UI: Gradio

Deployment: (Optional: Streamlit, Flask, or Hugging Face Spaces)

🤖 Sample Prediction
Input: "This product exceeded my expectations!"
Predicted Sentiment: 💚 Positive

Input: "Worst experience ever. Wouldn't recommend."
Predicted Sentiment: 💔 Negative

git clone https://github.com/Bluechip369-coder/sentiment-analysis.git
cd sentiment-analysis
pip install -r requirements.txt
python app.py



